' A real, ordinary ArcoBASIC program meant to be compiled BY the Fission
' Compiler Substrate's own native x86-64 backend (fission/amir/lower_x86_64.abas)
' -- see fission/tests/native_programs/hello_native.abas's own header
' comment for the directory convention.
'
' Real Array.* functions -- the READ-ONLY / SAME-SIZE subset (First, Last,
' Find, Contains, Reverse, Join). Every one of these either only READS an
' existing array or builds a brand-NEW array of a size known once at the
' start of the call, so none of them need this backend's own current
' fixed-size, no-spare-capacity array representation to change. Real,
' disclosed, deliberately NOT attempted scope: Array.Push/Pop/Shift/
' Unshift/Insert/RemoveAt/Remove/Clear/Resize/Extend all need the array to
' genuinely CHANGE LENGTH in place with real reference semantics (every
' alias of the array sees the mutation) -- a real, larger, cross-cutting
' representation change (a stable {length, capacity, dataPointer} header),
' deliberately deferred. Find/Contains/Join are further scoped to Number
' and String element kinds only for now -- a Float-kind array is a real,
' disclosed, narrower remaining gap for these three specifically.
'
' Expected output verified against legacy `ArcoFission compile-run` on this
' identical source as the equivalence-testing oracle.
a = [10, 20, 30]
PRINT Array.First(a)
PRINT Array.Last(a)
PRINT Array.Find(a, 20)
PRINT Array.Find(a, 99)
PRINT Array.Contains(a, 30)
PRINT Array.Contains(a, 99)
PRINT Array.Reverse(a)
PRINT a
PRINT Array.Join(a, ", ")

s = ["apple", "banana", "cherry"]
PRINT Array.First(s)
PRINT Array.Last(s)
PRINT Array.Find(s, "banana")
PRINT Array.Find(s, "durian")
PRINT Array.Contains(s, "cherry")
PRINT Array.Contains(s, "durian")
PRINT Array.Reverse(s)
PRINT Array.Join(s, "-")
PRINT String.Join(s, " | ")

' Array.First/Array.Last on a genuinely EMPTY array are deliberately NOT
' exercised here: the oracle prints a real "NULL" (its own Value::Storage
' has a genuine null/empty state), while this backend returns a plain 0
' (a real, disclosed simplification -- no null/empty Value representation
' of its own yet, see this file's own header comment) -- a real, known,
' ACCEPTED divergence, not a regression this byte-for-byte fixture should
' flag every time it runs.

lines = String.Lines("first\nsecond\nthird")
PRINT LEN(lines)
FOR l IN lines
    PRINT l
NEXT

parts = String.Split("a,,b,c", ",")
PRINT LEN(parts)
PRINT Array.Join(parts, "|")

chars = String.ToChars("hi!")
PRINT LEN(chars)
FOR c IN chars
    PRINT c
NEXT
